"""Think-SFT + cue answers 230 of the 328 harder problems right when allowed 32,768 generated tokens, against 207 when
the same answers are cut off at 16,384: 91 of its 93 cut-off answers end on their own, and 23 of them are right.

The page of one finding, served at /finding/cut-off-is-unfinished (view.py serves every tools/finding_<slug>.py) and
reached from its tile on /findings, which ICON draws. The picture is one lit plate. On it, each of the 328 answers of one
run is one thin horizontal bar whose length is the number of tokens it generated, sorted by length (shortest at the top),
on an axis of generated tokens from 0 to 32,768. A bar is blue when the answer ended within the allowance and is right,
grey when it ended and is wrong, and red up to the allowance when it was cut off there; the rest of a cut-off answer is a
faint line to its true end. The counts sit in the empty space above the long bars: right answers of 328 (the large
number), answers cut off, and generated tokens per problem. The one control is a slider, the tokens allowed per answer,
continuous from 16,384 to 32,768: the same stored answers are scored at any allowance (an answer counts as right at
allowance L when it ended within L tokens, was not cut off at 32,768, and grader v3 scored it right). As the allowance
moves right, the cut-off bars reach their end one by one and take the colour of their outcome. A quiet switch shows RL's
run instead; the bars travel to RL's order and lengths. A click on a bar shows that problem, its token count, its outcome
at 16,384, at the chosen allowance and at 32,768, and the stored end of the answer, for both models.
Address: /finding/cut-off-is-unfinished#[t<tokens>/][rl/][<panel or p<problem>>]; the default, Think-SFT + cue at 32,768,
is left out. An empty address opens at 16,384 and travels to 32,768. The rules are in .claude/skills/finding-page/SKILL.md;
the looks are those of tools/architecture.py (.claude/skills/site-ui/SKILL.md). The finding is board item result-c8b994
(work-ceccc0).

The artifacts are on main: the readout studies/rlneurons/results/cap32/readout.json and its run folders (commit c3481f1),
the per-problem rows results/cap32/rows-01/ (commit 10fc0f5, written by analysis/cap32_rows.py from the jobs' raw
answers, which are not in git), and the section 'Token cap 32,768 on the 328' of studies/rlneurons/README.md. PROBLEMS
below is built from the rows and the problem texts of the 328; every count on the page is computed from PROBLEMS. The
deployed site ships only tools/*.py, so the data is a literal; running this file compares it with the artifacts.

    PYTHONPATH=. uv run --no-project --with numpy python tools/finding_cut_off_is_unfinished.py
        checks DATA and PROBLEMS against the readout, the rows, the run folders and RL's earlier samples, and recomputes
        the paired bootstrap intervals
    ... python tools/finding_cut_off_is_unfinished.py --write    rewrites PROBLEMS from the rows
"""
